/*  FUNCTION NAME:      SCANLEAD
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Exclusive (lead) scan: emits the accumulator entering each step. out[1] is seed; out[i] is fn folded over the first i-1 elements. The clean replacement for the PREV(x, FALSE) + SCAN offset trick.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array: accumulator entering each step, starting with seed, same orientation as the input
    PARAMETERS:
        seed            (Required) Starting accumulator — becomes the first emitted value.
        array           (Required) 1-D values to fold over. Vertical or horizontal; the result matches the orientation.
        fn              (Required) LAMBDA(acc, current) returning the new accumulator.
    EXAMPLE:            =SCANLEAD(0, {10;20;30}, LAMBDA(a, v, a + v)) -> {0;10;30} (running total BEFORE each element)
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-07-01  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-08-24  Claude      Eta-wrap the user function before passing it as a MAP/SCAN/REDUCE/GROUPBY callback, so relative cell refs in lambda closures survive (#343)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
SCANLEAD = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [seed],
    [array],
    [fn],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        wasRow, AND(ROWS(array) = 1, COLUMNS(array) > 1),
        flat, TOCOL(array),
        full, SCAN(seed, flat, LAMBDA(acc_, x_, fn(acc_, x_))),
        col, IF(ROWS(flat) = 1, seed, VSTACK(seed, DROP(full, -1))),
        result, IF(wasRow, TRANSPOSE(col), col),
        result
)
);
